<article class="env-remark" id="06J6">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06J6">Remark <span data-tag="06J6">90.16.5</span>.</a> When $\mathcal{F}$ is cofibered in sets, condition (RS) is exactly condition (H4) from Schlessinger's paper <span class="cite">[<span class="postnote">Theorem 2.11</span>, <a href="/bibliography/Sch">Sch</a>]</span>. Namely, for a functor $F: \mathcal{C}_\Lambda \to \textit{Sets}$, condition (RS) states: If $A_1 \to A$ and $A_2 \to A$ are maps in $\mathcal{C}_\Lambda $ with $A_2 \to A$ surjective, then the induced map $F(A_1 \times _ A A_2) \to F(A_1) \times _{F(A)} F(A_2)$ is bijective. </p>
</article>